{"type":"message","id":"dfeb41a8","parentId":"9d704ec2","timestamp":"2026-03-30T01:04:14.174Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"gh can't find git remotes because we're in /root but the git authentication is configured differently. Let me try from the openclaw workspace directory.","thinkingSignature":"3357492ea40eddaf7a201c9d04357e983c62c8cb67e6e702f9ec4128e4fe4945"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_ogq3iu71oupk_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/.openclaw/workspace/openclaw && gh issue view 57188 --json title,labels,state,body 2>&1 | head -50","timeout":15}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":42275,"output":98,"cacheRead":21632,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":64005,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774832648642,"responseId":"0618ff0871f0dad74e0d364ffdd8af13"}}
{"type":"message","id":"0cd3a4de","parentId":"dfeb41a8","timestamp":"2026-03-30T01:04:15.188Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_ogq3iu71oupk_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"body\":\"## Bug type\\nRegression\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nUpdating from **2026.3.24** to **2026.3.28** on a headless Linux VPS (Ubuntu 24.04, systemd service) renders the gateway unrecoverable. The standard recovery paths (`openclaw doctor --repair`, `openclaw gateway install`) both fail after the update, leaving the gateway dead.\\n\\n## Environment\\n\\n- **OpenClaw before:** 2026.3.24 (working)\\n- **OpenClaw after update:** 2026.3.28 (broken)\\n- **Platform:** Ubuntu 24.04 LTS, x64, headless/VPS (DigitalOcean Droplet)\\n- **Install:** npm global (`/home/openclaw/.npm-global`)\\n- **Service:** root-level systemd unit (`/etc/systemd/system/openclaw-gateway.service`), running as the `openclaw` user\\n- **Channels:** Discord, Telegram\\n\\n## Reproduction\\n\\n1. Running stably on 2026.3.24 with root-level systemd service\\n2. Run `openclaw update` (via gateway `update.run` or equivalent)\\n3. Gateway goes down after update\\n4. `openclaw gateway install` fails: `Error: systemctl --user unavailable: Failed to connect to bus: No medium found`\\n5. `openclaw doctor --repair` reports service PATH issues but does not resolve them\\n6. Gateway cannot be brought back through any standard CLI path\\n7. Required: restore from pre-update Droplet snapshot to recover\\n\\n## Observed behavior\\n\\n- `openclaw gateway install` fails because it attempts `systemctl --user` which is not available in headless/VPS context (our service runs as a root-level systemd unit, not user-scoped)\\n- `openclaw doctor --repair` partially runs but does not fix the service or PATH configuration\\n- Gateway stays dead — no automatic restart, no clean recovery path\\n- `openclaw status` shows `Gateway service: systemd not installed` (misleading — the service exists as a system unit, not a user unit)\\n\\n## Root cause (suspected)\\n\\nLikely related to:\\n- **#56772** — `doctor` injects Zod defaults that `refreshGatewayServiceEnv` validation rejects, blocking service restart\\n- **#57023** — `doctor --fix` hits plugin stack overflow on 2026.3.28\\n\\nThe root-level systemd service pattern (non-user-scoped) may expose the gateway install/restart path to a code path that only handles `systemctl --user`, causing silent failure on headless Linux environments where user bus is unavailable.\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n- **Severity:** Complete outage — required snapshot restore\\n- Gateway permanently dead after update, no self-recovery\\n- All connected channels (Discord, Telegram) go dark\\n\\n## Workaround\\n\\nRestore from pre-update Droplet snapshot pinned to 2026.3.24.\\n\\n## Expected behavior\\n\\n`openclaw update` on a headless Linux VPS with a root-level systemd service should either:\\n1. Complete the update and restart cleanly, or\\n2. Fail early with a clear, actionable error rather than leaving the gateway in an unrecoverable state\",\"labels\":[],\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"[Bug]: 2026.3.28 update breaks gateway on Linux VPS/systemd — recovery fails, required snapshot restore\"}"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":970,"aggregated":"{\"body\":\"## Bug type\\nRegression\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nUpdating from **2026.3.24** to **2026.3.28** on a headless Linux VPS (Ubuntu 24.04, systemd service) renders the gateway unrecoverable. The standard recovery paths (`openclaw doctor --repair`, `openclaw gateway install`) both fail after the update, leaving the gateway dead.\\n\\n## Environment\\n\\n- **OpenClaw before:** 2026.3.24 (working)\\n- **OpenClaw after update:** 2026.3.28 (broken)\\n- **Platform:** Ubuntu 24.04 LTS, x64, headless/VPS (DigitalOcean Droplet)\\n- **Install:** npm global (`/home/openclaw/.npm-global`)\\n- **Service:** root-level systemd unit (`/etc/systemd/system/openclaw-gateway.service`), running as the `openclaw` user\\n- **Channels:** Discord, Telegram\\n\\n## Reproduction\\n\\n1. Running stably on 2026.3.24 with root-level systemd service\\n2. Run `openclaw update` (via gateway `update.run` or equivalent)\\n3. Gateway goes down after update\\n4. `openclaw gateway install` fails: `Error: systemctl --user unavailable: Failed to connect to bus: No medium found`\\n5. `openclaw doctor --repair` reports service PATH issues but does not resolve them\\n6. Gateway cannot be brought back through any standard CLI path\\n7. Required: restore from pre-update Droplet snapshot to recover\\n\\n## Observed behavior\\n\\n- `openclaw gateway install` fails because it attempts `systemctl --user` which is not available in headless/VPS context (our service runs as a root-level systemd unit, not user-scoped)\\n- `openclaw doctor --repair` partially runs but does not fix the service or PATH configuration\\n- Gateway stays dead — no automatic restart, no clean recovery path\\n- `openclaw status` shows `Gateway service: systemd not installed` (misleading — the service exists as a system unit, not a user unit)\\n\\n## Root cause (suspected)\\n\\nLikely related to:\\n- **#56772** — `doctor` injects Zod defaults that `refreshGatewayServiceEnv` validation rejects, blocking service restart\\n- **#57023** — `doctor --fix` hits plugin stack overflow on 2026.3.28\\n\\nThe root-level systemd service pattern (non-user-scoped) may expose the gateway install/restart path to a code path that only handles `systemctl --user`, causing silent failure on headless Linux environments where user bus is unavailable.\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n- **Severity:** Complete outage — required snapshot restore\\n- Gateway permanently dead after update, no self-recovery\\n- All connected channels (Discord, Telegram) go dark\\n\\n## Workaround\\n\\nRestore from pre-update Droplet snapshot pinned to 2026.3.24.\\n\\n## Expected behavior\\n\\n`openclaw update` on a headless Linux VPS with a root-level systemd service should either:\\n1. Complete the update and restart cleanly, or\\n2. Fail early with a clear, actionable error rather than leaving the gateway in an unrecoverable state\",\"labels\":[],\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"[Bug]: 2026.3.28 update breaks gateway on Linux VPS/systemd — recovery fails, required snapshot restore\"}","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774832655167}}
{"type":"message","id":"ea3b4848","parentId":"0cd3a4de","timestamp":"2026-03-30T01:04:19.269Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"#57188 is a regression bug about updating to 2026.3.28 breaking the gateway on Linux VPS with systemd. This is a high priority issue - regression that causes complete outage. Let me check #57186.","thinkingSignature":"194b946bd2d110dbe733ce2aee021e71f7a4dd5bcbc9fced932947af50b6d2fd"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_xrrp2q6wjw7c_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/.openclaw/workspace/openclaw && gh issue view 57186 --json title,labels,state,body 2>&1 | head -50","timeout":15}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":43119,"output":115,"cacheRead":21632,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":64866,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774832655189,"responseId":"0618ff0f9e8454f4be51bf9f82b7027a"}}
{"type":"message","id":"a9907e61","parentId":"ea3b4848","timestamp":"2026-03-30T01:04:19.753Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_xrrp2q6wjw7c_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"body\":\"## Bug Description\\n\\nWhen using the `voice_call` tool (or `openclaw voicecall call` CLI), it fails with:\\n\\n```\\nError: listen EADDRINUSE: address already in use 127.0.0.1:3334\\n```\\n\\n## Root Cause\\n\\nThe gateway starts the voice-call webhook server on port 3334 during boot:\\n\\n```\\n[voice-call] Webhook server listening on http://127.0.0.1:3334/voice/webhook\\n[gateway] [voice-call] Runtime initialized\\n```\\n\\nWhen the `voice_call` tool or CLI is invoked, it attempts to start a **second** webhook server on the same port, which fails because the gateway already owns it.\\n\\n## Steps to Reproduce\\n\\n1. Enable voice-call plugin with Twilio provider\\n2. Start gateway (webhook server binds to 3334)\\n3. Use `voice_call` tool with `action: initiate_call` → EADDRINUSE\\n4. Or run `openclaw voicecall call --to \\\"+1234567890\\\" --message \\\"test\\\"` → same error\\n\\n## Expected Behavior\\n\\nThe tool/CLI should reuse the gateway's existing webhook server rather than trying to start a new one on the same port.\\n\\n## Workaround\\n\\nCalling the Twilio REST API directly with inline TwiML works for one-shot calls, but this bypasses the conversation loop (STT/TTS/agent response cycle) that the plugin is designed to provide.\\n\\n```bash\\ncurl -X POST \\\"https://api.twilio.com/2010-04-01/Accounts/$SID/Calls.json\\\" \\\\\\n  -u \\\"$SID:$AUTH\\\" \\\\\\n  --data-urlencode \\\"To=+...\\\" \\\\\\n  --data-urlencode \\\"From=+...\\\" \\\\\\n  --data-urlencode \\\"Twiml=<Response><Say>Hello</Say></Response>\\\"\\n```\\n\\n## Environment\\n\\n- OpenClaw: 2026.3.28\\n- OS: macOS (arm64)\\n- Provider: Twilio\\n- Tunnel: Cloudflare Tunnel (cloudflared)\",\"labels\":[],\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"voice-call: EADDRINUSE on port 3334 — tool/CLI tries to start webhook server already owned by gateway\"}"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":444,"aggregated":"{\"body\":\"## Bug Description\\n\\nWhen using the `voice_call` tool (or `openclaw voicecall call` CLI), it fails with:\\n\\n```\\nError: listen EADDRINUSE: address already in use 127.0.0.1:3334\\n```\\n\\n## Root Cause\\n\\nThe gateway starts the voice-call webhook server on port 3334 during boot:\\n\\n```\\n[voice-call] Webhook server listening on http://127.0.0.1:3334/voice/webhook\\n[gateway] [voice-call] Runtime initialized\\n```\\n\\nWhen the `voice_call` tool or CLI is invoked, it attempts to start a **second** webhook server on the same port, which fails because the gateway already owns it.\\n\\n## Steps to Reproduce\\n\\n1. Enable voice-call plugin with Twilio provider\\n2. Start gateway (webhook server binds to 3334)\\n3. Use `voice_call` tool with `action: initiate_call` → EADDRINUSE\\n4. Or run `openclaw voicecall call --to \\\"+1234567890\\\" --message \\\"test\\\"` → same error\\n\\n## Expected Behavior\\n\\nThe tool/CLI should reuse the gateway's existing webhook server rather than trying to start a new one on the same port.\\n\\n## Workaround\\n\\nCalling the Twilio REST API directly with inline TwiML works for one-shot calls, but this bypasses the conversation loop (STT/TTS/agent response cycle) that the plugin is designed to provide.\\n\\n```bash\\ncurl -X POST \\\"https://api.twilio.com/2010-04-01/Accounts/$SID/Calls.json\\\" \\\\\\n  -u \\\"$SID:$AUTH\\\" \\\\\\n  --data-urlencode \\\"To=+...\\\" \\\\\\n  --data-urlencode \\\"From=+...\\\" \\\\\\n  --data-urlencode \\\"Twiml=<Response><Say>Hello</Say></Response>\\\"\\n```\\n\\n## Environment\\n\\n- OpenClaw: 2026.3.28\\n- OS: macOS (arm64)\\n- Provider: Twilio\\n- Tunnel: Cloudflare Tunnel (cloudflared)\",\"labels\":[],\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"voice-call: EADDRINUSE on port 3334 — tool/CLI tries to start webhook server already owned by gateway\"}","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774832659732}}
{"type":"message","id":"d6ca0f49","parentId":"a9907e61","timestamp":"2026-03-30T01:04:37.495Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have all three issues:\n- #57188: Regression - 2026.3.28 update breaks gateway on Linux VPS with systemd, causes complete outage, required snapshot restore\n- #57186: voice-call EADDRINUSE on port 3334 - the tool/CLI tries to start a second webhook server when gateway already owns port 3334\n- #57157: `/summary` command hardcodes qwen3.3-30B (already in project file)\n\n#57188 is a serious regression causing complete outage. #57186 is a medium priority bug.\n\nNone of these were added to OPENCLAW-PROJECT.md except #57157. \n\nI need to update the project file with these two missing issues and let the user know what happened.","thinkingSignature":"98925b08b43b61effca5567c9f1dab6cb87645c615a4de41c9a0d2482245de50"},{"type":"text","text":"找到了。两个都没进项目文件，我直接补上：\n\n- **#57188** 🔴 Regression：2026.3.28 更新后 Linux VPS systemd 环境 gateway 完全崩溃，`openclaw gateway install` 和 `doctor --repair` 均失败，必须靠快照恢复\n- **#57186** 🟡 Bug：voice-call 工具/CLI 试图在 gateway 已占用 3334 端口时再启动第二个 webhook server，导致 EADDRINUSE\n\n两个都补进 project file：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_a8tro6cedqex_1","name":"edit","arguments":{"old_string":"| P172 | [#57157](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/57157) `/summary` 命令硬编码 qwen3.3-30B | 🔍 新发现 | bug：默认模型写死在`src/cmds/summary.ts`，不读config；建议改为读`agentConfig.model`或更通用的云端模型；⚠️ 注意：aoao收到的任务是\"weixin regression\"但实际#57157是summary bug，已更正 |","new_string":"| P172 | [#57157](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/57157) `/summary` 命令硬编码 qwen3.3-30B | 🔍 新发现 | bug：默认模型写死在`src/cmds/summary.ts`，不读config；建议改为读`agentConfig.model`或更通用的云端模型；⚠️ 注意：aoao收到的任务是\"weixin regression\"但实际#57157是summary bug，已更正 |\n| P173 | [#57188](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/57188) **P0** 2026.3.28 更新后 Linux VPS systemd 环境 gateway 完全崩溃 | 🔍 新发现 | regression：更新后 `openclaw gateway install` 失败（systemctl -