{"type":"message","id":"fb7f0917","parentId":"4b1cce0d","timestamp":"2026-03-30T11:09:53.304Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. Now let me update P189 to add a note about #57551 being complex. But actually, let me focus on what's most important.\n\nThe user asked me to simplify the task and follow up on whether aoao times out again. The last aoao task was to fix #57551, which timed out again. \n\nI should:\n1. Acknowledge to the user that #57551 is a complex fix that aoao is struggling with\n2. Note that #57626 is already covered by PR #57455 from the community\n3. Suggest either trying a different approach for #57551 or moving to simpler issues\n\nLet me give a clear status update to the user.","thinkingSignature":"696122e428ed9aee5c11ccf9c7fbcab16ef39081e9511c2f12520bc0437ad604"},{"type":"text","text":"**当前状态更新：**\n\n**aoao 情况**（按你的要求跟进）：\n- #57626 修复：❌ 失败（没有 PR，代码未提交）\n- **重要发现**：社区已有人提交 **PR #57455**（fix/ollama: parse stringified tool call arguments），基本覆盖了 #57626 的问题，无需重复提交\n\n**aoao 对 #57551（Kimi 无限重试）持续超时**：\n- 根因分析是对的（attempt.ts 里的 retry 逻辑把参数验证错误当作可重试错误）\n- 但文件编辑操作一直超时，无法完成 commit\n\n**建议**：\n1. #57551 是深层参数序列化 bug，治本需要改 retry 策略架构，复杂\n2. 可以先支持社区 PR，或等社区有人修\n3. 换一个更简单的 issue 来修（比如 #57622 Web UI 不自动滚动、#57623 memoryFlush 问题）\n\n要我继续派 aoao 试 #57551，还是换更简单的？"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":95185,"output":355,"cacheRead":21632,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":117172,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774868980288,"responseId":"06198cf4a2df3b7f9162372ab6fe382b"}}
{"type":"message","id":"cd4c0c9c","parentId":"fb7f0917","timestamp":"2026-03-30T11:18:09.451Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Mon 2026-03-30 19:13 GMT+8] 4方向扫描报告 [2026-03-30 18:55 CST]\n\nGitHub: 发现了1个新issue（#57660 - Telegram polling stall detector fires too aggressively）+ 5个PRs（#51476 #55619 #57655 #57516 #57650）\nInStreet: 无\nDiscord: 无\n插件: 无\n\n结论：#57660 是本次扫描发现的唯一新issue，Telegram polling stall detector 过于激进（110s timeout）导致消息投递失败。可修性 S，值得研究 polling stall detector 的超时逻辑。"}],"timestamp":1774869489372,"provenance":{"kind":"inter_session","sourceSessionKey":"agent:xixi:cron:6f8bd6c8-5b5f-4cf7-8e6f-3479fd23fc64","sourceTool":"sessions_send"}}}
{"type":"message","id":"8e344bb4","parentId":"cd4c0c9c","timestamp":"2026-03-30T11:18:19.963Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"xixi sent the scan report. Let me process it and decide what to do.\n\nKey findings:\n- #57660 (new): Telegram polling stall detector fires too aggressively (110s timeout)\n- 5 new PRs: #51476, #55619, #57655, #57516, #57650\n\nThe xixi scan ran at 18:55 but the cron was showing error \"Message failed\" at 18:55. However, xixi did send this report via sessions_send. \n\nThe report shows:\n- #57660: Telegram polling stall detector fires too aggressively - 110s timeout causes message delivery failure\n\n\n- This looks like a legitimate P2 issue worth investigating, so I'll add it to the project file and route it to aoao.","thinkingSignature":"153fc18002cb6e806b7f247eb3c3720b09203dad4002fc55dafc15f391da0c1a"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_xrc2vp3d7cpe_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/.openclaw/workspace/openclaw && gh issue view 57660 --json title,body,labels 2>&1 | head -30","timeout":15}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":80,"output":228,"cacheRead":9465,"cacheWrite":104342,"totalTokens":114115,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774869489452,"responseId":"06198ef1f097e1f2b6c08e63682ea7c4"}}
{"type":"message","id":"be9160f1","parentId":"8e344bb4","timestamp":"2026-03-30T11:18:20.485Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_xrc2vp3d7cpe_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"body\":\"### Bug type\\n\\nBehavior bug (incorrect output/state without crash)\\n\\n### Beta release blocker\\n\\nNo\\n\\n### Summary\\n\\nTelegram polling stall detector fires at 110s, restarting the gateway mid-message-generation and causing message delivery failures\\n\\n### Steps to reproduce\\n\\n1. Send a Telegram message to an OpenClaw bot that requires >110 seconds to process (e.g., complex query, research task)\\n2. Wait for response — observe it may not arrive\\n3. Check journalctl logs: find \\\"Polling stall detected (no getUpdates for XXXs)\\\" followed by gateway restart\\n4. During restart window, ALL Telegram API calls fail for 3-7 minutes\\n\\n### Expected behavior\\n\\nThe Telegram polling should not restart the gateway when processing a message that takes longer than 110 seconds. The stall threshold should be configurable and set to a value that accommodates real-world LLM response times (typically 60-300s for complex queries).\\n\\n### Actual behavior\\n\\nThe Telegram polling stall detector fires at ~110 seconds of inactivity. When a message takes >110s to process, the gateway restarts mid-generation. During the restart, ALL Telegram API calls fail with \\\"Network request failed\\\" for 3-7 minutes. After restart completes, connectivity recovers. This cycle repeats every time a message takes >110s to process.\\n\\n### OpenClaw version\\n\\n2026.3.24\\n\\n### Operating system\\n\\nUbuntu 24.04 (Linux 6.17)\\n\\n### Install method\\n\\nnpm global (Node.js v24.13.1)\\n\\n### Model\\n\\nminimax/MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed\\n\\n### Provider / routing chain\\n\\nOpenClaw (local gateway) -> Telegram Bot API\\n\\n### Additional provider/model setup details\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Logs, screenshots, and evidence\\n\\n```shell\\n\\n```\\n\\n### Impact and severity\\n\\nAffected: Telegram users on OpenClaw v2026.3.24\\nSeverity: High (blocks workflow — messages not delivered)\\nFrequency: Intermittent — fires whenever a message takes >110s to process\\nConsequence: Users do not receive AI responses; must resend message after gateway restarts\\n\\n### Additional information\\n\\nThe stall threshold (currently ~110s, hardcoded) is too short for production use with LLM-powered agents. Request:\\n1. Make the stall threshold configurable via openclaw.json (e.g., channels.telegram.stallThreshold: 300)\\n2. Increase the default threshold to at least 300 seconds (5 minutes) to accommodate typical LLM response times\\n\\nWorkaround applied: streaming: \\\"partial\\\" set to \\\"off\\\" to reduce API call volume during failure windows. This is a partial mitigation only.\",\"labels\":[{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACQomLZw\",\"name\":\"bug\",\"description\":\"Something isn't working\",\"color\":\"d73a4a\"},{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACZxxN7g\",\"name\":\"bug:behavior\",\"description\":\"Incorrect behavior without a crash\",\"color\":\"D73A4A\"}],\"title\":\"[Bug]: Telegram polling stall detector fires too aggressively (110s), causes message delivery failures\"}"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":477,"aggregated":"{\"body\":\"### Bug type\\n\\nBehavior bug (incorrect output/state without crash)\\n\\n### Beta release blocker\\n\\nNo\\n\\n### Summary\\n\\nTelegram polling stall detector fires at 110s, restarting the gateway mid-message-generation and causing message delivery failures\\n\\n### Steps to reproduce\\n\\n1. Send a Telegram message to an OpenClaw bot that requires >110 seconds to process (e.g., complex query, research task)\\n2. Wait for response — observe it may not arrive\\n3. Check journalctl logs: find \\\"Polling stall detected (no getUpdates for XXXs)\\\" followed by gateway restart\\n4. During restart window, ALL Telegram API calls fail for 3-7 minutes\\n\\n### Expected behavior\\n\\nThe Telegram polling should not restart the gateway when processing a message that takes longer than 110 seconds. The stall threshold should be configurable and set to a value that accommodates real-world LLM response times (typically 60-300s for complex queries).\\n\\n### Actual behavior\\n\\nThe Telegram polling stall detector fires at ~110 seconds of inactivity. When a message takes >110s to process, the gateway restarts mid-generation. During the restart, ALL Telegram API calls fail with \\\"Network request failed\\\" for 3-7 minutes. After restart completes, connectivity recovers. This cycle repeats every time a message takes >110s to process.\\n\\n### OpenClaw version\\n\\n2026.3.24\\n\\n### Operating system\\n\\nUbuntu 24.04 (Linux 6.17)\\n\\n### Install method\\n\\nnpm global (Node.js v24.13.1)\\n\\n### Model\\n\\nminimax/MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed\\n\\n### Provider / routing chain\\n\\nOpenClaw (local gateway) -> Telegram Bot API\\n\\n### Additional provider/model setup details\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Logs, screenshots, and evidence\\n\\n```shell\\n\\n```\\n\\n### Impact and severity\\n\\nAffected: Telegram users on OpenClaw v2026.3.24\\nSeverity: High (blocks workflow — messages not delivered)\\nFrequency: Intermittent — fires whenever a message takes >110s to process\\nConsequence: Users do not receive AI responses; must resend message after gateway restarts\\n\\n### Additional information\\n\\nThe stall threshold (currently ~110s, hardcoded) is too short for production use with LLM-powered agents. Request:\\n1. Make the stall threshold configurable via openclaw.json (e.g., channels.telegram.stallThreshold: 300)\\n2. Increase the default threshold to at least 300 seconds (5 minutes) to accommodate typical LLM response times\\n\\nWorkaround applied: streaming: \\\"partial\\\" set to \\\"off\\\" to reduce API call volume during failure windows. This is a partial mitigation only.\",\"labels\":[{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACQomLZw\",\"name\":\"bug\",\"description\":\"Something isn't working\",\"color\":\"d73a4a\"},{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACZxxN7g\",\"name\":\"bug:behavior\",\"description\":\"Incorrect behavior without a crash\",\"color\":\"D73A4A\"}],\"title\":\"[Bug]: Telegram polling stall detector fires too aggressively (110s), causes message delivery failures\"}","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774869500460}}
{"type":"message","id":"50e6f9db","parentId":"be9160f1","timestamp":"2026-03-30T11:18:30.833Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a clear bug with:\n- Steps to reproduce\n- Clear root cause (hardcoded 110s stall detector)\n- Suggested fix (make configurable, increase default to 300s)\n- Impact: High - messages not delivered\n- Labels: bug, bug:behavior\n\nThis is a good candidate for aoao to fix. The fix should be:\n1. Make stall threshold configurable via openclaw.json\n2. Increase default to 300s\n\nLet me派 aoao to fix this. But remember - aoao keeps timing out on file editing tasks. However, for a relatively simple fix like changing a hardcoded timeout to a config value, it might be more manageable.\n\n\nI'll dispatch this to aoao with a tight scope—just locate the hardcoded 110s value in the Telegram polling code, add the config option, and set the new default to 300s.","thinkingSignature":"32c3cfbdb6e1c1b561720dcdee68093a446dd2399ef2b64686c66df76ee005b8"},{"type":"text","text":"#57660 根因清晰、修复简单，值得派 aoao。这个我直接派：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_ojsy0whxkan5_1","name":"sessions_send","arguments":{"sessionKey":"agent:aoao:feishu:aoao:direct:ou_0dee72e5f9e6a83b0555fdfd161f2506","message":"任务：修复 #57660（只做调研+结论，不写代码）\n\n问题：Telegram polling stall detector 硬编码 110s，导致 >110s 的消息处理被网关重启打断\n\n只做调研，输出3条：\n1. 硬编码 110s 的代码文件路径和行号\n2. stall threshold 当前配置方式（是否已有配置项）\n3. 修复方案（怎么改成可配置的 + 默认值改多少）\n\n完成后直接回复这3条。","timeoutSeconds":300}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":93428,"output":382,"cacheRead":21397,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":115207,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774869500486,"responseId":"06198efc68779ee5f5291c53bef2abf2"}}
