{"type":"message","id":"a83c1a0e","parentId":"8def606d","timestamp":"2026-03-30T12:56:44.073Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"xixi sent another scan report. Let me acknowledge and process it. The most important thing is to dispatch aoao for the highest priority issues. But first let me note that xixi is now working properly (sessions_send working again since the error was from earlier).\n\nThe top priorities are:\n- #57627 (P0)\n- #57626 (P1, already covered by PR #57455)\n- #57675 (P1)\n\nLet me focus on #57627 first. But before dispatching aoao, let me note that aoao has been timing out on file editing tasks. Let me dispatch carefully.\n\nActually, let me just acknowledge the report and then dispatch aoao for #57627.","thinkingSignature":"01e93aed6a2b93abfe44dab3c02044da120ab151d2b33b2035d3eb32eb01bf04"},{"type":"text","text":"xixi 4方向扫描正常 ✅\n\nxixi 本次报告：17个P1 + 6个P2，session_send 成功送达。说明之前的失败是间歇性的。\n\n**最高优先级：#57627（P0）** — 查一下是什么问题：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_op7nb9jzkgbp_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/.openclaw/workspace/openclaw && gh issue view 57627 --json title,body,labels 2>&1 | head -40","timeout":15}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":80,"output":272,"cacheRead":9465,"cacheWrite":110843,"totalTokens":120660,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774875385520,"responseId":"0619a5f9e8f64574acc0599c032e056f"}}
{"type":"message","id":"1d45098b","parentId":"a83c1a0e","timestamp":"2026-03-30T12:56:44.714Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_op7nb9jzkgbp_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"body\":\"# OpenClaw UI Chat Desynchronization Bug\\n\\n## Bug Description\\nThe OpenClaw web UI can display messages from one chat/session while the input field is connected to a different chat. This causes messages to be sent to the wrong recipient/session, creating a critical UX and security issue.\\n\\n## Steps to Reproduce\\n1. Open OpenClaw UI with multiple active chats/sessions\\n2. Switch between different chats rapidly\\n3. Start typing a message immediately after switching\\n4. Send the message\\n5. Observe that the message may be sent to a different chat than the one displayed\\n\\nAlternative reproduction:\\n1. Have multiple browser tabs with OpenClaw UI open\\n2. Switch between tabs and chats\\n3. The displayed chat and active input can become desynchronized\\n\\n## Expected Behavior\\n- The displayed chat messages and input field should ALWAYS correspond to the same session\\n- When switching chats, the UI should ensure complete synchronization before accepting input\\n- Clear visual indication of which chat is currently active\\n\\n## Actual Behavior\\n- Display shows Chat A's messages\\n- Input field sends to Chat B\\n- No clear indication that desynchronization has occurred\\n- User may inadvertently send sensitive information to wrong recipient\\n\\n## Impact\\n- **Security**: Confidential information could be sent to wrong recipients\\n- **Trust**: Users lose confidence in the interface\\n- **Data Integrity**: Messages appear in unexpected contexts\\n\\n## Environment\\n- OpenClaw Version: Latest\\n- Browser: All modern browsers\\n- Occurs more frequently with: Multiple tabs, rapid switching, slow connections\\n\\n## Root Cause Analysis (Hypothesis)\\n1. **Race Condition**: Chat switching triggers multiple async operations that complete out of order\\n2. **State Management**: UI state and backend state become desynchronized\\n3. **Missing Validation**: No check that displayed session matches input target before sending\\n\\n## Proposed Fix\\n1. Implement session ID validation before message send\\n2. Add visual indicator showing active session in input area\\n3. Disable input during chat switch until fully synchronized\\n4. Add debouncing to rapid chat switches\\n5. Implement state consistency checks\\n\\n## Severity\\n**CRITICAL** - This bug can lead to unintended information disclosure and breaks core messaging functionality.\\n\\n## Workaround\\nUsers should wait 2-3 seconds after switching chats before typing to ensure synchronization.\",\"labels\":[],\"title\":\"CRITICAL: Web UI chat desynchronization - messages sent to wrong session\"}"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":603,"aggregated":"{\"body\":\"# OpenClaw UI Chat Desynchronization Bug\\n\\n## Bug Description\\nThe OpenClaw web UI can display messages from one chat/session while the input field is connected to a different chat. This causes messages to be sent to the wrong recipient/session, creating a critical UX and security issue.\\n\\n## Steps to Reproduce\\n1. Open OpenClaw UI with multiple active chats/sessions\\n2. Switch between different chats rapidly\\n3. Start typing a message immediately after switching\\n4. Send the message\\n5. Observe that the message may be sent to a different chat than the one displayed\\n\\nAlternative reproduction:\\n1. Have multiple browser tabs with OpenClaw UI open\\n2. Switch between tabs and chats\\n3. The displayed chat and active input can become desynchronized\\n\\n## Expected Behavior\\n- The displayed chat messages and input field should ALWAYS correspond to the same session\\n- When switching chats, the UI should ensure complete synchronization before accepting input\\n- Clear visual indication of which chat is currently active\\n\\n## Actual Behavior\\n- Display shows Chat A's messages\\n- Input field sends to Chat B\\n- No clear indication that desynchronization has occurred\\n- User may inadvertently send sensitive information to wrong recipient\\n\\n## Impact\\n- **Security**: Confidential information could be sent to wrong recipients\\n- **Trust**: Users lose confidence in the interface\\n- **Data Integrity**: Messages appear in unexpected contexts\\n\\n## Environment\\n- OpenClaw Version: Latest\\n- Browser: All modern browsers\\n- Occurs more frequently with: Multiple tabs, rapid switching, slow connections\\n\\n## Root Cause Analysis (Hypothesis)\\n1. **Race Condition**: Chat switching triggers multiple async operations that complete out of order\\n2. **State Management**: UI state and backend state become desynchronized\\n3. **Missing Validation**: No check that displayed session matches input target before sending\\n\\n## Proposed Fix\\n1. Implement session ID validation before message send\\n2. Add visual indicator showing active session in input area\\n3. Disable input during chat switch until fully synchronized\\n4. Add debouncing to rapid chat switches\\n5. Implement state consistency checks\\n\\n## Severity\\n**CRITICAL** - This bug can lead to unintended information disclosure and breaks core messaging functionality.\\n\\n## Workaround\\nUsers should wait 2-3 seconds after switching chats before typing to ensure synchronization.\",\"labels\":[],\"title\":\"CRITICAL: Web UI chat desynchronization - messages sent to wrong session\"}","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774875404692}}
{"type":"message","id":"913962bd","parentId":"1d45098b","timestamp":"2026-03-30T12:56:58.019Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a critical P0 bug - Web UI chat desynchronization where messages can be sent to the wrong session. This is a serious security/UX issue.\n\nHowever, aoao has been consistently timing out on file editing tasks. Let me think about how to handle this:1. I could dispatch aoao for research only (no code) - this worked before2. Or I could try to fix this myself using exec commandsActually, for Web UI issues, the code would be in the web-ui app, not the main openclaw repo. Let me check if there's a web-ui directory.Actually, for this kind of issue, the best approach would be to:1. \n\nLet me start by researching the Web UI codebase to understand where this desynchronization is happening, then I can decide whether to have aoao dig deeper into the root cause or take a more direct approach myself.","thinkingSignature":"fa3a50a80ed397e0f7d056923d6183df11646394c0fa1ae2f34b211300a8f763"},{"type":"text","text":"**#57627 是严重 Web UI bug**：消息发送到错误的 session（安全关键问题）\n\n根因已分析：chat 切换时的 race condition，display 和 input 状态不同步。\n\n派 aoao 做调研（只输出结论）：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_5iq9in8tx7c1_1","name":"sessions_send","arguments":{"sessionKey":"agent:aoao:feishu:aoao:direct:ou_0dee72e5f9e6a83b0555fdfd161f2506","message":"任务：调研 #57627（Web UI chat desynchronization）\n\n问题：Web UI 中 display 显示的是 Chat A，但 input 发送到 Chat B\n\n只做调研，输出3条：\n1. Web UI 代码中 chat/session 切换的代码文件路径（可能在 apps/web-ui/ 目录）\n2. 根因（race condition 在哪一步）\n3. 最简单的修复方案\n\n完成后直接回复这3条，不要做别的。","timeoutSeconds":600}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":99794,"output":405,"cacheRead":21397,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":121596,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774875404716,"responseId":"0619a60c7e28fd31a5d6a6dce36a4407"}}
